powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "description": "Returns the plug-in's own refusal to the browser instead of the platform's generic \"Common Data Service error occurred.\" Without it every refusal on this site reaches the page as that one sentence and a 400, whatever it was: the review submit's list of unanswered required questions, the edit-conflict prompt, the sign-off and regrade preconditions. Every friendlyError on the site reads error.innererror.message and was written for this setting, which had never been created - reported 2026-09-13, against a submit that named the one question left unanswered in the plug-in trace and told the checker nothing. Documented default is False. Safe here because these messages are written to be read by the person who hit them: they carry a VALIDATION, PRECONDITION, CONFLICT or UNAUTHORIZED prefix, say what to do next, and never expose a table name, query, id or stack trace (PP-16). The pages cap anything else at 300 characters.",
  "value": "true"
}
